    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d869">

                <pb facs="1016" n="936" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg936"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tower to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-09-17"><hi rendition="#italic">September 17,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 601.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of the unnumbered dispatch of Mr. Adee, Acting Secretory of State, dated the
                    12th of August, 1902, in which he inclosed to me your circular letter<anchor
                        n="a" xml:id="d869-f1"/> dated <pb facs="1017" n="937" xml:id="pg937"/> the
                    11th of August, in regard to the condition of Jews in Roumania, with two
                    additional printed copies of that letter.</p>
                <p>In compliance with your instructions I sought an interview with Count Lamsdorff,
                    Imperial Russian minister for foreign affairs, to whom I presented the subject,
                    and to whom, upon his request, I handed one of the printed copies of your
                    circular letter.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charlemagne
                    Tower.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
